desc:FMA Sub-Air
// @version 1.7.0
// @author Free Mix Audio
// @changelog
//   v1.7.0 (2026-10-22)
//     - NEW GUI (Juan's design, measured 1:1 from his layered PSD):
//       the window is now exactly the metal plate, 951x623 - the
//       dark surround is gone. Every control sits at its PSD
//       position and size: MONO BELOW is back to its designed
//       proportion (75% of a main knob), chrome bat-toggle levers
//       and POWER bat from the PSD layers, IN/GR/OUT and DE-HARSH
//       at their new places. Knob draw sizes are computed from
//       the measured disc inside each filmstrip (the classic
//       strips carry the disc at ~122 px inside 154 px frames),
//       so every knob lands at its exact PSD diameter.
//     - NEW: LOW CUT (slider17) - stepped high-pass, OFF then
//       20..200 Hz in 20 Hz steps (11 detents), green pointer knob
//       between SUB ENHANCE and TIGHT. End of chain, post-sum,
//       before the safety limiter, so the limiter stops reacting
//       to infrasonics and drive-generated DC. Slopes follow the
//       per-mode standard: BUS 12 dB/oct (2nd-order Butterworth),
//       INST 18 dB/oct (3rd-order Butterworth). TPT/SVF structure,
//       ~15 ms coefficient slew + ~10 ms engage crossfade (no
//       clicks, no zipper); 0 = exact bypass.
//   v1.6.0 (2026-10-20)
//     - Clean reworked: zone-shaped knob authority (internal
//       SOFT 0-50% / MID 50-83% / HARD 83-100% zones), gated by
//       AIR (Clean only polices the boost once AIR passes ~half,
//       soft knee in), with mode ceilings: INST may eat the whole
//       boost on harsh peaks; BUS caps the reduction at 3 dB so a
//       mix bus or master can never be torn apart. Clean still
//       only reduces the AIR boost, never the source itself.
//     - De-harsh detector thresholds lowered for sensitivity:
//       BUS -24 dBFS, INST -32 dBFS (were -18 / -26).
//     - DE-HARSH LED: new eager law. It lights early and climbs
//       fast with detector activity and knob position - a livelier
//       visual than the gentle real reduction behind it.
//     - New vu_off.png (companion graphics): the needle now rests
//       parked at the left stop when powered off instead of
//       disappearing.
//     - Mouse wheel: every knob and lever (incl. MODE, OPERATION
//       and POWER) answers to the scroll wheel, one step per notch;
//       levers are directional - scroll up/down drives them to their
//       ends and holds them there. Only the IN/GR/OUT meter selector
//       stays click-only.
//   v1.5.9 (2026-10-17)
//     - Fixed VU level followers (IN and OUT): the old one-pole
//       follower chased the instantaneous rectified signal instead
//       of holding the peak, so on a steady sine it settled
//       ~0.6 dB below the true peak at every level (measured:
//       0 -> -0.6, -6 -> -6.6, -12 -> -12.6 dB). The followers
//       now hold the peak and decay multiplicatively (150 ms
//       release), the same form as the peak meters: residual
//       sine ripple <= 0.07 dB. Needle smoothing and the scale
//       mapping are unchanged.
//   v1.5.8 (2026-10-10)
//     - New OPERATION switch (BUS/INST) with horizontal 2-pos lever,
//       placed symmetrically opposite the DE-HARSH LED:
//       BUS mode (left): 160 Hz sub crossover, -18 dBFS de-harsh
//         threshold, standard drive voicing — for mix bus and mastering.
//       INST mode (right): 90 Hz sub crossover, -26 dBFS de-harsh
//         threshold (creative tool, LED responds on normal material),
//         warmer drive voicing (stronger even-harmonic emphasis) —
//         for individual instruments and tracks.
//   v1.5.7 (2026-10-10)
//     - Fixed sub crossover: the highpass section used 3 biquads
//       (6th-order) instead of 2 (4th-order), breaking the Linkwitz-Riley
//       reconstruction and causing a ~5 dB dip at ~154 Hz whenever the
//       sub section was engaged. Now true LR4 4th-order on both bands.
//   v1.5.6 (2026-10-09)
//     - VU face graphics corrected: scale graduation now matches
//       the needle programming exactly.
//   v1.5.5 (2026-10-09)
//     - VU meter ballistics: dedicated level follower with 5ms attack
//       and 150ms release (Tukan-style), plus asymmetric needle smoothing
//       (fast attack 0.75, smooth release 0.35) for analog feel.
//   v1.5.4 (2026-10-09)
//     - Reduced hit area on the 4 levers (SUB BYPASS,
//       SAFETY LIMITER, AIR BYPASS, DRIVE POWER) and on the
//       MODE selector: now ±48px horizontal and 565-614 vertical,
//       fitted to the graphic edge. POWER unchanged.
//   v1.5.3 (2026-10-09)
//     - Code cleanup: removed obsolete comments
//       (references to previous design sizes and "preview build").
//   v1.5.2 (2026-10-09)
//     - Fixed @gfx block order: the size declaration
//       (@gfx 1024 700) is now the first instruction in the section,
//       so REAPER opens the window at the correct size.
//   v1.5.1 (2026-10-09)
//     - VU Meter Mode now defaults to IN (was GR).
//   v1.5 (2026-10-09)
//     - Display name simplificado a "FMA Sub-Air" (sin número de versión)
//       para evitar conflictos en futuras actualizaciones. La versión
//       se sigue controlando vía @version para ReaPack.
//   v1.4 (2026-10-04)
//     - NEW: Vintage Drive saturator — warm tube-style even-harmonic
//       saturation ("silk" voicing: asymmetric triode-like curve, ultra-soft
//       knee, subtlety-first). Red DRIVE knob (0% = transparent) plus
//       FOCUS selector (Sub / Full / Air) so the user chooses which band
//       gets saturated. 2x oversampled saturation path for alias-free
//       harmonics. Drive power switch (ON = processing).
//   v1.3 (2026-10-01)
//     - GUI controls now update the DSP in real time (no need to press play)
//     - Per-section bypass switches respond instantly
//   v1.2
//     - Initial FMA Series release
// @about
//   # FMA Sub-Air
//   Mastering-grade sub & air sculptor with Vintage Drive saturator.
//   FMA Series by Free Mix Audio.
//   Free for students and friends of Free Mix Audio.
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/panel.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_marron.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_hueso.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_naranja.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_rojo.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_monobelow.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_lowcut.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/toggle_2pos.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/mode_3pos.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/power_2pos.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/led_verde_fs.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/led_amarillo_fs.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/vu_face.png
// @provides fma-sub-air_gfx/vu_off.png
// @screenshot https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FMA-Series/fma-reapack/main/screenshots/fma-sub-air.png
// @link https://www.facebook.com/freemixaudio
//=============================================================================
// FMA Sub-Air -- mastering sub & air sculptor + Vintage Drive
// FMA Series · Free Mix Audio
// (c) 2026 Free Mix Audio. All rights reserved.
//
// A mastering-grade low/high sculptor with safety guardrails:
//   SUB section -- gentle sub enhance, transient punch, sub-to-mono
//   AIR section -- smooth air shelf with dynamic de-harsh ("Clean")
//   DRIVE section (NEW v1.4) -- Vintage Drive: warm tube-style saturator,
//                  even-harmonic dominant ("silk" voicing, triode-like
//                  asymmetric curve, ultra-soft knee). Red DRIVE knob,
//                  FOCUS selector (Sub/Full/Air), 2x oversampled.
//   MASTER      -- input/output trims, independent section bypass,
//                  output safety limiter (fixed -1 dBFS ceiling),
//                  in/out + limiter-GR metering
//
// Design notes (CPU-conscious):
//   * Shelves are built as dry + g*filtered (one-pole) blends: no per-sample
//     biquad coefficient updates, no zipper noise, trivial cost.
//   * Biquads are only used where steepness matters (sub extraction @160 Hz,
//     mono-ize lowpass, presence bandpass) and their coefficients are
//     computed in @slider / upd_params(), never in @sample.
//   * The Vintage Drive band-split reuses the 160 Hz LR4 coefficients and
//     the 8 kHz one-pole highpass corner (coherent with Sub Enhance / Air).
//   * Drive saturation runs at 2x (short FIR oversampling, delay-compensated
//     wet path) to keep harmonics alias-free; the dry path is untouched.
//   * All applied gains are one-pole smoothed in @sample (click-free).
//   * ALL time constants are srate-independent: filter corners use
//     2*pi*f/srate and every envelope/smoothing coefficient is built with
//     smc(tau_seconds), so ballistics are identical at 44.1/48/88.2/96 kHz.
//     Internal processing is 64-bit throughout (EEL2 doubles).
//   * NaN/Inf sanitising on input and output; periodic denormal flush.
//
// v1.4 (2026-10-04):
//   * NEW Vintage Drive saturator section (DSP + panel in the v1.3 UI
//     style; the full vintage PNG interface follows in Phase 2).
//   * Drive power switch uses ON = processing (no "bypass" double negative).
//
// v1.3 (2026-10-01):
//   * Real-time GUI control: parameter changes made from the custom GUI
//     now call upd_params() immediately (previously the derived values
//     only refreshed when REAPER next fired @slider, e.g. on Play).
//     Section bypasses engage/disengage instantly.
//   * New rescalable GUI: neon identity from the Free Mix Audio logo,
//     all-English labels with short explanations of every control.
//   * desc bumped to v1.3. DSP path unchanged from v1.2 (44/44 verified).
//
// NOTE (EEL2 rule, verified empirically): @init must come before any
// `function` definitions, otherwise calls from @slider/@sample silently
// fail to compile. This matches all stock Cockos JSFX.
//=============================================================================


slider1:0<-12,12,0.1>Input Gain (dB)
slider2:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>SUB Bypass
slider3:0<0,100,1>Sub Enhance (%) - sub weight
slider4:0<0,100,1>Tight (%) - transient punch
slider5:0<0,4,1{Off,60,80,100,120}>Mono Below (Hz)
slider6:0<0,1,1{On,Off}>Safety Limiter
slider7:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>AIR Bypass
slider8:0<0,6,0.1>Air (dB) - high shelf
slider9:0<0,100,1>Clean (%) - de-harsh
slider10:0<-12,12,0.1>Output Gain (dB)
slider11:0<0,100,1>Drive (%) - vintage saturation
slider12:1<0,2,1{Sub,Full,Air}>Drive Focus
slider13:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Drive Power
slider14:0<0,2,1{IN,GR,OUT}>VU Meter Mode
slider15:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Power
slider16:0<0,1,1{Bus,Inst}>-Operation
slider17:0<0,200,20>-Low Cut (Hz)

// pi is NOT a built-in EEL2 constant (reads as 0); stock plugins define
// it themselves, so we set it here before anything uses it.
//---------------------------------------------------------------- @init
filename:0,fma-sub-air_gfx/panel.png
filename:1,fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_marron.png
filename:2,fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_hueso.png
filename:3,fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_naranja.png
filename:4,fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_rojo.png
filename:5,fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_monobelow.png
filename:6,fma-sub-air_gfx/toggle_2pos.png
filename:7,fma-sub-air_gfx/mode_3pos.png
filename:8,fma-sub-air_gfx/vu_face.png
filename:9,fma-sub-air_gfx/power_2pos.png
filename:10,fma-sub-air_gfx/led_verde_fs.png
filename:11,fma-sub-air_gfx/led_amarillo_fs.png
filename:12,fma-sub-air_gfx/vu_off.png
filename:13,fma-sub-air_gfx/knob_lowcut.png
@init
  pi = 3.141592653589793;
  in_g = 1; out_g = 1;          // smoothed applied gains
  enh_g = 0; bamt = 0; red_db = 0; inst_mode = 0; xover_f = 160;
  gr = 1; gr_disp = 1;          // limiter gain (1 = no reduction)
  ef = 0; es = 0; harsh = 0;    // envelope followers
  m_in = 0; m_out = 0; cnt = 0; // meters / flush counter
  vu_in_sm = 0; vu_out_sm = 0; // VU ballistics smoothers
  drag_id = -1;                 // GUI drag state
  g_f0 = 0; g_f1 = 0; g_f2 = 0; g_fdh = 0; g_dh_peak = 0; g_dh_last = -1;  // LED fades
  bypass_mix = 0;  // 0=wet, 1=dry
  lc_g = 0; lc_k = 1.4142135623730951; lc_3m = 0; lc_mix = 0;  // Low Cut smoothed state
  ui_sliders = 0;               // generic sliders hidden (gfx UI only)
  startup = 0;                  // startup fade (masks cold-start transients)
  slider_show(131071, 0);        // hide all 15 generic sliders in the FX window
  // (all filter states default to 0)

  // ---- Vintage Drive state ----
  drvw = 0; drvpush = 1;        // smoothed wet blend / saturation push
  // 2x oversampling via polyphase FIR (no circular buffers: EEL2's &
  // misbehaves on negative floats in this build). 17-tap halfband
  // Hamming-windowed sinc, fc=0.25 of the 2x rate: -37dB at 30kHz,
  // -55dB at Nyquist. Srate-independent. Scalar coefficients (verified);
  // all delay histories are plain scalars (zero-init). Even taps are
  // zero except the center (halfband) so the even phase is a scaled delay.
  // Odd taps renormalized so odd-phase sum == even-phase sum (prevents
  // Nyquist ripple from phase gain mismatch).
  df1 = -0.0052574513455552;  df3 = 0.0232920444723720;
  df5 = -0.0763712451093941;  df7 = 0.3087717982711559;
  df8 = 0.5008702925771572;   df9 = 0.3087717982711560;
  df11 = -0.0763712451093942; df13 = 0.0232920444723720;
  df15 = -0.0052574513455552;
  // (all history/delay states below default to 0)

//---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers
function lp_coefs(f) (
  // 2nd-order Butterworth lowpass -> bq_* globals (unnormalised)
  w0 = 2*pi*f/srate; cw = cos(w0); al = sin(w0)*0.7071067811865476;
  bq_b0 = (1-cw)*0.5; bq_b1 = 1-cw; bq_b2 = (1-cw)*0.5;
  bq_a0 = 1+al;       bq_a1 = -2*cw; bq_a2 = 1-al;
);

function bp_coefs(f, q) (
  // bandpass, constant 0 dB peak gain -> bq_* globals (unnormalised)
  w0 = 2*pi*f/srate; cw = cos(w0); al = sin(w0)/(2*q);
  bq_b0 = al; bq_b1 = 0; bq_b2 = -al;
  bq_a0 = 1+al; bq_a1 = -2*cw; bq_a2 = 1-al;
);

function hp_coefs(f) (
  // 2nd-order Butterworth highpass -> bq_* globals (unnormalised)
  w0 = 2*pi*f/srate; cw = cos(w0); al = sin(w0)*0.7071067811865476;
  bq_b0 = (1+cw)*0.5; bq_b1 = -(1+cw); bq_b2 = (1+cw)*0.5;
  bq_a0 = 1+al;       bq_a1 = -2*cw;   bq_a2 = 1-al;
);

function smc(tau_s) (
  // one-pole smoothing coefficient for an absolute time constant tau_s
  // (seconds). Same ballistics at ANY srate.
  1 - exp(-1/(tau_s*srate));
);

function upd_params() (
  // Recompute everything the DSP derives from the sliders. Called from
  // @slider (REAPER-driven changes) AND from the GUI handlers the moment
  // a control is touched, so GUI edits always apply in real time.
  in_t    = 2^(slider1/6);
  out_t   = 2^(slider10/6);
  sub_byp = slider2 > 0.5;
  air_byp = slider7 > 0.5;
  enh_g_t = 10^(slider3*0.075/20) - 1;   // Sub Enhance 0..100% -> 0..+7.5 dB
  punch01 = slider4*0.01;
  mono_sel = slider5|0;
  mono_f = mono_sel == 1 ? 60 : mono_sel == 2 ? 80 :
           mono_sel == 3 ? 100 : mono_sel == 4 ? 120 : 80;
  mono_t  = mono_sel > 0 ? 1 : 0;
  // sub section is bit-transparent when no sub processing is dialed in
  // (avoids crossover phase/magnitude ripple in the neutral path)
  sub_active = (slider3 > 0) || (slider4 > 0) || (mono_sel > 0);
  safety_on = slider6 < 0.5;
  air_db  = slider8;
  clean01 = slider9*0.01;

  // ---- Vintage Drive ----
  drv01    = slider11*0.01;
  drv_focus = slider12|0;              // 0=Sub, 1=Full, 2=Air
  drv_on   = slider13 > 0.5;          // power: ON = processing
  // whole stage skipped unless the user actually dials drive in, so the
  // neutral path stays bit-transparent (no added latency either)
  drv_active = drv_on && (slider11 > 0);
  // silk-zone mapping: smoothstep -> first third = micro-saturation,
  // upper range opens to obvious warmth
  damt = drv01*drv01*(3 - 2*drv01);
  drvw_t   = damt;                    // wet blend 0..1
  drvpush_t = 1 + damt*24;            // saturation push 1..25
  // triode-like asymmetry (tune by ear/measurement): positive knee
  // harder than negative -> even-harmonic dominant. Stronger ratio
  // keeps H2 > H3 even at mid drive (silk voicing).
  drv_ap = inst_mode ? 1.3 : 1.6;   // Inst: warmer | Bus: standard
  drv_an = inst_mode ? 0.35 : 0.28;
  // DC-blocker coefficient (~10 Hz, srate-independent): the asymmetric
  // saturator generates DC; remove it aggressively (only affects the
  // saturated harmonics, not the dry fundamental in the wet/dry blend)
  ddc_r = exp(-2*pi*10/srate);

  // one-pole coefficients (depend on srate only)
  c_lp55 = exp(-2*pi*55/srate);        // sub-enhance shelf corner
  c_hp8k = exp(-2*pi*8000/srate);      // air shelf corner

  // srate-independent smoothing (absolute time constants)
  sm_gain  = smc(0.01134);   // param/mono-blend smoothing
  sm_5ms   = smc(0.005);     // tight fast envelope
  sm_50ms  = smc(0.050);     // tight slow envelope
  sm_100ms = smc(0.100);     // limiter release
  sm_fast  = smc(0.0004535); // GR meter + clean attack
  sm_1ms   = smc(0.001134);  // harsh attack
  sm_113ms = smc(0.113);     // harsh release
  mdec     = exp(-1/(0.04534*srate));  // peak-meter decay
  vu_rel   = exp(-1/(0.150*srate));     // VU release 150ms (peak-hold decay)

  // sub crossover: Linkwitz-Riley 4th-order
  // Bus mode: 160 Hz | Inst mode: 90 Hz
  inst_mode = slider16 > 0.5;
  xover_f = inst_mode ? 90 : 160;
  lp_coefs(xover_f);
  s_b0 = bq_b0/bq_a0; s_b1 = bq_b1/bq_a0; s_b2 = bq_b2/bq_a0;
  s_a1 = bq_a1/bq_a0; s_a2 = bq_a2/bq_a0;
  hp_coefs(xover_f);
  sh_b0 = bq_b0/bq_a0; sh_b1 = bq_b1/bq_a0; sh_b2 = bq_b2/bq_a0;
  sh_a1 = bq_a1/bq_a0; sh_a2 = bq_a2/bq_a0;

  // mono-ize: Butterworth HP @mono_f on the sub-band side channel
  hp_coefs(mono_f);
  mh_b0 = bq_b0/bq_a0; mh_b1 = bq_b1/bq_a0; mh_b2 = bq_b2/bq_a0;
  mh_a1 = bq_a1/bq_a0; mh_a2 = bq_a2/bq_a0;

  // presence bandpass @4.5 kHz, Q=1 (harshness detector)
  bp_coefs(4500, 1);
  p_b0 = bq_b0/bq_a0; p_b1 = bq_b1/bq_a0; p_b2 = bq_b2/bq_a0;
  p_a1 = bq_a1/bq_a0; p_a2 = bq_a2/bq_a0;

  // ---- Low Cut (v1.7.0): stepped HPF at the very end of the chain.
  // fc comes straight from slider17 (0 = OFF). Slope follows the
  // per-mode standard: BUS 2nd-order Butterworth (12 dB/oct, SVF
  // k = sqrt(2)); INST 3rd-order Butterworth (18 dB/oct, SVF k = 1
  // plus the TPT one-pole section, blended in by lc_3m in @sample).
  lc_hz = slider17|0;
  lc_on = lc_hz > 0;
  lc_g_t = lc_on ? tan(pi*lc_hz/srate) : 0;
  lc_k_t = inst_mode ? 1 : 1.4142135623730951;
  lc_3rd = inst_mode;
  sm_lc = smc(0.015);    // coefficient slew: click-free step changes
  sm_lcm = smc(0.010);   // engage/disengage crossfade
);

function drv_sat(x) (
  // Vintage Drive "silk" saturator core (runs at 2x rate).
  // Asymmetric rational soft clipper: different positive/negative knees
  // (triode-like) -> even-harmonic dominant. Ultra-soft knee, unity
  // small-signal gain, bounded output. drvpush/drv_ap/drv_an are globals
  // refreshed by upd_params() / smoothed in @sample.
  ax = x*drvpush;
  a = ax >= 0 ? drv_ap : drv_an;
  ax/(1 + a*abs(ax));
);

function flush_all() (  // denormal guard, called every 1024 samples (cheap)
  abs(s_y1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (s_y1_0 = 0);  abs(s_y2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (s_y2_0 = 0);
  abs(s_y1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (s_y1_1 = 0);  abs(s_y2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (s_y2_1 = 0);
  abs(s2_y1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (s2_y1_0 = 0);  abs(s2_y2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (s2_y2_0 = 0);
  abs(s2_y1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (s2_y1_1 = 0);  abs(s2_y2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (s2_y2_1 = 0);
  abs(sh_y1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh_y1_0 = 0);  abs(sh_y2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh_y2_0 = 0);
  abs(sh_y1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh_y1_1 = 0);  abs(sh_y2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh_y2_1 = 0);
  abs(sh2_y1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh2_y1_0 = 0);  abs(sh2_y2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh2_y2_0 = 0);
  abs(sh2_y1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh2_y1_1 = 0);  abs(sh2_y2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh2_y2_1 = 0);
  abs(sh3_y1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh3_y1_0 = 0);  abs(sh3_y2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh3_y2_0 = 0);
  abs(sh3_y1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh3_y1_1 = 0);  abs(sh3_y2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (sh3_y2_1 = 0);
  abs(h_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (h_y1 = 0);  abs(h_y2) < 0.000000000001 ? (h_y2 = 0);
  abs(h2_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (h2_y1 = 0);  abs(h2_y2) < 0.000000000001 ? (h2_y2 = 0);
  abs(h3_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (h3_y1 = 0);  abs(h3_y2) < 0.000000000001 ? (h3_y2 = 0);
  abs(h4_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (h4_y1 = 0);  abs(h4_y2) < 0.000000000001 ? (h4_y2 = 0);
  abs(h5_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (h5_y1 = 0);  abs(h5_y2) < 0.000000000001 ? (h5_y2 = 0);
  abs(h6_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (h6_y1 = 0);  abs(h6_y2) < 0.000000000001 ? (h6_y2 = 0);
  abs(e_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (e_0 = 0);        abs(e_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (e_1 = 0);
  abs(p_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (p_y1 = 0);      abs(p_y2) < 0.000000000001 ? (p_y2 = 0);
  abs(ef) < 0.000000000001 ? (ef = 0);          abs(es) < 0.000000000001 ? (es = 0);
  abs(harsh) < 0.000000000001 ? (harsh = 0);
  // Vintage Drive states
  abs(dl_x1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_x1_0 = 0);  abs(dl_x2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_x2_0 = 0);
  abs(dl_y1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_y1_0 = 0);  abs(dl_y2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_y2_0 = 0);
  abs(dl2_x1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_x1_0 = 0);  abs(dl2_x2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_x2_0 = 0);
  abs(dl2_y1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_y1_0 = 0);  abs(dl2_y2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_y2_0 = 0);
  abs(dl_x1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_x1_1 = 0);  abs(dl_x2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_x2_1 = 0);
  abs(dl_y1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_y1_1 = 0);  abs(dl_y2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl_y2_1 = 0);
  abs(dl2_x1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_x1_1 = 0);  abs(dl2_x2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_x2_1 = 0);
  abs(dl2_y1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_y1_1 = 0);  abs(dl2_y2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dl2_y2_1 = 0);
  abs(dah_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dah_0 = 0);  abs(dahx_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dahx_0 = 0);
  abs(dah_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dah_1 = 0);  abs(dahx_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dahx_1 = 0);
  abs(ddc_x0) < 0.000000000001 ? (ddc_x0 = 0);  abs(ddc_y0) < 0.000000000001 ? (ddc_y0 = 0);
  abs(ddc_x1) < 0.000000000001 ? (ddc_x1 = 0);  abs(ddc_y1) < 0.000000000001 ? (ddc_y1 = 0);
  // polyphase histories + delay lines (plain scalars)
  abs(dux0_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux0_0 = 0);  abs(dux1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux1_0 = 0);
  abs(dux2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux2_0 = 0);  abs(dux3_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux3_0 = 0);
  abs(dux4_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux4_0 = 0);  abs(dux5_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux5_0 = 0);
  abs(dux6_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux6_0 = 0);
  abs(dux0_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux0_1 = 0);  abs(dux1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux1_1 = 0);
  abs(dux2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux2_1 = 0);  abs(dux3_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux3_1 = 0);
  abs(dux4_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux4_1 = 0);  abs(dux5_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux5_1 = 0);
  abs(dux6_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dux6_1 = 0);
  abs(dse0_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse0_0 = 0);  abs(dse1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse1_0 = 0);
  abs(dse2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse2_0 = 0);  abs(dse3_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse3_0 = 0);
  abs(dse4_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse4_0 = 0);  abs(dse5_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse5_0 = 0);
  abs(dse6_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse6_0 = 0);  abs(dse7_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse7_0 = 0);
  abs(dso0_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso0_0 = 0);  abs(dso1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso1_0 = 0);
  abs(dso2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso2_0 = 0);  abs(dso3_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso3_0 = 0);
  abs(dso4_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso4_0 = 0);  abs(dso5_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso5_0 = 0);
  abs(dso6_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso6_0 = 0);  abs(dso7_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso7_0 = 0);
  abs(dse0_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse0_1 = 0);  abs(dse1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse1_1 = 0);
  abs(dse2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse2_1 = 0);  abs(dse3_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse3_1 = 0);
  abs(dse4_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse4_1 = 0);  abs(dse5_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse5_1 = 0);
  abs(dse6_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse6_1 = 0);  abs(dse7_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dse7_1 = 0);
  abs(dso0_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso0_1 = 0);  abs(dso1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso1_1 = 0);
  abs(dso2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso2_1 = 0);  abs(dso3_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso3_1 = 0);
  abs(dso4_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso4_1 = 0);  abs(dso5_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso5_1 = 0);
  abs(dso6_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso6_1 = 0);  abs(dso7_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dso7_1 = 0);
  abs(dzz0_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz0_0 = 0);  abs(dzz1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz1_0 = 0);
  abs(dzz2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz2_0 = 0);  abs(dzz3_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz3_0 = 0);
  abs(dzz0_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz0_1 = 0);  abs(dzz1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz1_1 = 0);
  abs(dzz2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz2_1 = 0);  abs(dzz3_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dzz3_1 = 0);
  abs(dbb0_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb0_0 = 0);  abs(dbb1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb1_0 = 0);
  abs(dbb2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb2_0 = 0);  abs(dbb3_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb3_0 = 0);
  abs(dbb0_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb0_1 = 0);  abs(dbb1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb1_1 = 0);
  abs(dbb2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb2_1 = 0);  abs(dbb3_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (dbb3_1 = 0);
  // Low Cut states
  abs(lc_ic1_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (lc_ic1_0 = 0);  abs(lc_ic2_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (lc_ic2_0 = 0);
  abs(lc_lp_0) < 0.000000000001 ? (lc_lp_0 = 0);
  abs(lc_ic1_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (lc_ic1_1 = 0);  abs(lc_ic2_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (lc_ic2_1 = 0);
  abs(lc_lp_1) < 0.000000000001 ? (lc_lp_1 = 0);
);

//---------------------------------------------------------------- gfx helpers
// Design space: 720 x 440 units. The GUI computes a scale factor from the
// actual window size and draws everything proportionally (rescalable).
function dval(id) (
  id == 7 ? slider5 :
  id == 6 ? slider11 :
  id == 0 ? slider3 : id == 1 ? slider4 : id == 2 ? slider8 :
  id == 3 ? slider9 : id == 4 ? slider1 : slider10;
);
function dmin(id) ( (id == 4 || id == 5) ? -12 : 0; );  // id7: 0..4
function dmax(id) ( id == 2 ? 6 : id == 7 ? 4 : (id == 4 || id == 5) ? 12 : 100; );
function dspan(id) ( dmax(id) - dmin(id); );
function ddef(id) ( 0; );  // all gfx slider defaults are 0; mono-below reset -> Off
function dslider_of(id) (
  id == 7 ? 5 :
  id == 6 ? 11 :
  id == 0 ? 3 : id == 1 ? 4 : id == 2 ? 8 : id == 3 ? 9 : id == 4 ? 1 : 10;
);
function dset(id, v) (
  v = min(max(v, dmin(id)), dmax(id));
  id == 7 ? slider5 = floor(v + 0.5) :
  id == 6 ? slider11 = v :
  id == 0 ? slider3 = v : id == 1 ? slider4 = v : id == 2 ? slider8 = v :
  id == 3 ? slider9 = v : id == 4 ? slider1 = v : slider10 = v;
  sliderchange(dslider_of(id));
  upd_params();
);
function fstr(i) (
  // Drive FOCUS label -> #dtxt global (EEL2: no #string params/returns)
  i == 0 ? #dtxt = "SUB" : i == 1 ? #dtxt = "FULL" : #dtxt = "AIR";
);
// NOTE (EEL2 rule): #strings cannot be params/returns of plain functions
// (only methods/instance). Labels travel via the #dlbl / #dtxt globals.
function mstr(i) (
  i == 0 ? #dtxt = "Off" : i == 1 ? #dtxt = "60" : i == 2 ? #dtxt = "80" :
  i == 3 ? #dtxt = "100" : #dtxt = "120";
);
function dstr(id) (
  id == 7 ? mstr(slider5|0) :
  id == 6 ? sprintf(#dtxt, "%d %%", slider11|0) :
  id == 0 ? sprintf(#dtxt, "%d %%", slider3|0) :
  id == 1 ? sprintf(#dtxt, "%d %%", slider4|0) :
  id == 2 ? sprintf(#dtxt, "+%.1f dB", slider8) :
  id == 3 ? sprintf(#dtxt, "%d %%", slider9|0) :
  id == 4 ? sprintf(#dtxt, "%+.1f dB", slider1) :
            sprintf(#dtxt, "%+.1f dB", slider10);
);
//---------------------------------------------------------------- vintage UI helpers (Phase 2)
function hit_knob(mx, my, cx, cy, dia) (
  (mx-cx)*(mx-cx) + (my-cy)*(my-cy) < (dia*0.5+10)*(dia*0.5+10);
);
function click_toggle(mx, my, cx, cy, sn) (
  mx >= cx-80 && mx < cx+80 && my >= cy-26 && my < cy+26 ? (
    sn == 2 ? slider2 = 1 - (slider2 > 0.5) :
    sn == 6 ? slider6 = 1 - (slider6 > 0.5) :
    sn == 7 ? slider7 = 1 - (slider7 > 0.5) :
              slider13 = 1 - (slider13 > 0.5);
    sliderchange(sn); upd_params();
  );
);
function draw_vknob(img, isz, cx, cy, dia, id, pr, pg, pb) (
  norm = (dval(id) - dmin(id))/dspan(id);
  gfx_blit(img, 1, 0, 0, 0, isz, isz,
           g_ox + (cx - dia*0.5)*g_sc, g_oy + (cy - dia*0.5)*g_sc,
           dia*g_sc, dia*g_sc);
  ang = (-135 + 270*norm - 90)*$pi/180;
  px = g_ox + cx*g_sc; py = g_oy + cy*g_sc;
  gfx_set(pr, pg, pb);
  gfx_line(px + dia*0.16*g_sc*cos(ang), py + dia*0.16*g_sc*sin(ang),
           px + dia*0.40*g_sc*cos(ang), py + dia*0.40*g_sc*sin(ang), 1);
);
function draw_toggle(cx, cy, on) (  // slot baked into bg; handle drawn here
  ghx = on ? cx + 40 : cx - 40;
  gx0 = g_ox + (ghx-28)*g_sc; gy0 = g_oy + (cy-20)*g_sc;
  gfx_set(0.08, 0.07, 0.06); gfx_roundrect(gx0-2*g_sc, gy0-2*g_sc, 60*g_sc, 44*g_sc, 9*g_sc, 1);
  gfx_set(0.52, 0.49, 0.44); gfx_roundrect(gx0, gy0, 56*g_sc, 40*g_sc, 8*g_sc, 1);
  gfx_set(0.72, 0.69, 0.63); gfx_roundrect(gx0, gy0, 56*g_sc, 18*g_sc, 8*g_sc, 1);
  gfx_set(0.25, 0.23, 0.21); gfx_line(gx0+28*g_sc, gy0+5*g_sc, gx0+28*g_sc, gy0+35*g_sc, 1);
);
function draw_pushbtn(cx, cy, w, h, active) (  // caption via #dtxt
  gx0 = g_ox + (cx-w/2)*g_sc; gy0 = g_oy + (cy-h/2)*g_sc;
  active ? gfx_set(0.95, 0.60, 0.24) : gfx_set(0.30, 0.26, 0.22);
  gfx_roundrect(gx0-2*g_sc, gy0-2*g_sc, (w+4)*g_sc, (h+4)*g_sc, 7*g_sc, 1);
  gfx_set(0.09, 0.08, 0.07); gfx_roundrect(gx0, gy0, w*g_sc, h*g_sc, 6*g_sc, 1);
  gfx_set(0.15, 0.13, 0.11); gfx_roundrect(gx0, gy0, w*g_sc, h*g_sc*0.45, 6*g_sc, 1);
  active ? gfx_set(1.0, 0.80, 0.52) : gfx_set(0.80, 0.67, 0.46);
  gfx_setfont(3, "Arial", max(9, 19*g_sc));
  gfx_x = g_ox + cx*g_sc; gfx_y = g_oy + cy*g_sc;
  gfx_drawstr(#dtxt, 1|4|256);
);

// Knob ids: 0=INPUT 1=OUTPUT 2=CLEAN 3=SUB ENHANCE 4=TIGHT 5=AIR 6=DRIVE 7=MONO BELOW
function kval(id) (
  id==0 ? slider1 : id==1 ? slider10 : id==2 ? slider9 : id==3 ? slider3 :
  id==4 ? slider4 : id==5 ? slider8 : id==6 ? slider11 : id==7 ? slider5 : slider17/20;
);
function kmin(id) ( (id==0||id==1) ? -12 : 0; );
function kmax(id) ( id==0||id==1 ? 12 : id==5 ? 6 : id==7 ? 4 : id==8 ? 10 : 100; );
function kdef(id) ( 0; );
function kset(id, v) (
  v = min(max(v, kmin(id)), kmax(id));
  (id==7 || id==8) ? v = floor(v+0.5);
  id==0 ? slider1=v : id==1 ? slider10=v : id==2 ? slider9=v : id==3 ? slider3=v :
  id==4 ? slider4=v : id==5 ? slider8=v : id==6 ? slider11=v : id==7 ? slider5=v : slider17 = v*20;
  id==0 ? sliderchange(1) : id==1 ? sliderchange(10) : id==2 ? sliderchange(9) :
  id==3 ? sliderchange(3) : id==4 ? sliderchange(4) : id==5 ? sliderchange(8) :
  id==6 ? sliderchange(11) : id==7 ? sliderchange(5) : sliderchange(17);
  upd_params();
);
function kimg(id) (
  id==0 ? 1 : id==1 ? 1 : id==2 ? 2 : id==3 ? 3 :
  id==4 ? 3 : id==5 ? 2 : id==6 ? 4 : id==7 ? 5 : 13;
);
function kfs(id) ( id==7 ? 102 : id==8 ? 134 : 154; );
function kds(id) ( (id==0||id==1) ? 154.5 : id==6 ? 159.5 : id==7 ? 116.9 : id==8 ? 66.9 : 160.8; );
function kcx(id) (
  id==0 ? 146.2 : id==1 ? 808.2 : id==2 ? 709.7 : id==3 ? 146.5 :
  id==4 ? 364.5 : id==5 ? 589.7 : id==6 ? 808.7 : id==7 ? 248.6 : 257;
);
function kcy(id) (
  id==0 ? 113 : id==1 ? 113 : id==2 ? 258.3 : id==3 ? 410.8 :
  id==4 ? 409.8 : id==5 ? 410.3 : id==6 ? 410 : id==7 ? 255.7 : 487;
);
function kframe(id) (
  id==7 ? (slider5|0) : id==8 ? ((slider17/20)|0) :
  floor((kval(id)-kmin(id))/(kmax(id)-kmin(id))*127+0.5);
);
function hit_knob2(mx,my,cx,cy) (
  (mx-cx)*(mx-cx)+(my-cy)*(my-cy) < 64*64;
);
function draw_knob(id) (
  // The classic filmstrips carry the disc at 122-123 px inside their
  // 154 px frames (84/82 in the 102 MONO frame): kds() is the FRAME
  // size that makes the DISC land on its PSD diameter, and the small
  // kk_o offsets re-centre the disc (its centre inside the frame is
  // offset by ~1 px from the frame centre).
  kk_fr = min(max(kframe(id),0), id==7 ? 4 : id==8 ? 10 : 127);
  kk_fs = kfs(id); kk_ds = kds(id); kk_cx = kcx(id); kk_cy = kcy(id);
  kk_ox = (id==7 ? 0.31 : id==8 ? 0 : 0.26)*kk_ds/kk_fs;
  kk_oy = (id==7 ? 0.34 : id==8 ? 0 : 0.27)*kk_ds/kk_fs;
  gfx_blit(kimg(id), 1, 0, 0, kk_fr*kk_fs, kk_fs, kk_fs,
            g_px0+kk_cx-kk_ds/2+kk_ox, g_py0+kk_cy-kk_ds/2+kk_oy, kk_ds, kk_ds);
);
function draw_tog2(nx, ny, fr) (
  // Juan's stable-version filmstrip: 128 px frames, ring dia 66 centred
  // at (64.5, 63.5). Drawn at 87.3 so the ring lands on the PSD socket
  // diameter (~45). (nx, ny) = the ring centre on the canvas.
  gfx_blit(6, 1, 0, 0, fr*128, 128, 128, g_px0+nx-44, g_py0+ny-43.3, 87.3, 87.3);
);

@slider
  upd_params();

//---------------------------------------------------------------- @sample
@sample
  //--- POWER: save dry for bypass
  dry0 = spl0; dry1 = spl1;
  //--- sanitise inputs (kills NaN/Inf before they can propagate)
  spl0 = spl0 != spl0 ? 0 : min(max(spl0, -4), 4);
  spl1 = spl1 != spl1 ? 0 : min(max(spl1, -4), 4);

  in_g += (in_t - in_g)*sm_gain;
  x0 = spl0*in_g;
  x1 = spl1*in_g;
  m_in = max(m_in*mdec, max(abs(x0), abs(x1)));
  vu_pk = max(abs(x0), abs(x1));
  vu_in_sm = max(vu_pk, vu_in_sm*vu_rel);   // true peak hold + 150ms decay

  //================ SUB section ================
  (sub_byp || !sub_active) ? (
    y0 = x0; y1 = x1;
  ) : (
    // sub-band extraction: LR4 lowpass @160 Hz (two cascaded biquads
    // per channel), plus explicit LR4 highpass for the highs.
    t0 = s_b0*x0 + s_b1*s_x1_0 + s_b2*s_x2_0 - s_a1*s_y1_0 - s_a2*s_y2_0;
    s_x2_0 = s_x1_0; s_x1_0 = x0; s_y2_0 = s_y1_0; s_y1_0 = t0;
    sb0 = s_b0*t0 + s_b1*s2_x1_0 + s_b2*s2_x2_0 - s_a1*s2_y1_0 - s_a2*s2_y2_0;
    s2_x2_0 = s2_x1_0; s2_x1_0 = t0; s2_y2_0 = s2_y1_0; s2_y1_0 = sb0;
    t1 = s_b0*x1 + s_b1*s_x1_1 + s_b2*s_x2_1 - s_a1*s_y1_1 - s_a2*s_y2_1;
    s_x2_1 = s_x1_1; s_x1_1 = x1; s_y2_1 = s_y1_1; s_y1_1 = t1;
    sb1 = s_b0*t1 + s_b1*s2_x1_1 + s_b2*s2_x2_1 - s_a1*s2_y1_1 - s_a2*s2_y2_1;
    s2_x2_1 = s2_x1_1; s2_x1_1 = t1; s2_y2_1 = s2_y1_1; s2_y1_1 = sb1;
    // highs: LR4 highpass @160 Hz (two cascaded biquads per channel)
    u0 = sh_b0*x0 + sh_b1*sh_x1_0 + sh_b2*sh_x2_0 - sh_a1*sh_y1_0 - sh_a2*sh_y2_0;
    sh_x2_0 = sh_x1_0; sh_x1_0 = x0; sh_y2_0 = sh_y1_0; sh_y1_0 = u0;
    h0 = sh_b0*u0 + sh_b1*sh2_x1_0 + sh_b2*sh2_x2_0 - sh_a1*sh2_y1_0 - sh_a2*sh2_y2_0;
    sh2_x2_0 = sh2_x1_0; sh2_x1_0 = u0; sh2_y2_0 = sh2_y1_0; sh2_y1_0 = h0;
    u1 = sh_b0*x1 + sh_b1*sh_x1_1 + sh_b2*sh_x2_1 - sh_a1*sh_y1_1 - sh_a2*sh_y2_1;
    sh_x2_1 = sh_x1_1; sh_x1_1 = x1; sh_y2_1 = sh_y1_1; sh_y1_1 = u1;
    h1 = sh_b0*u1 + sh_b1*sh2_x1_1 + sh_b2*sh2_x2_1 - sh_a1*sh2_y1_1 - sh_a2*sh2_y2_1;
    sh2_x2_1 = sh2_x1_1; sh2_x1_1 = u1; sh2_y2_1 = sh2_y1_1; sh2_y1_1 = h1;

    // mono-ize: M/S on the sub band, steep HP on the side channel.
    mid_sb = (sb0 + sb1)*0.5;
    side_sb = (sb0 - sb1)*0.5;
    sh = mh_b0*side_sb + mh_b1*h_x1 + mh_b2*h_x2 - mh_a1*h_y1 - mh_a2*h_y2;
    h_x2 = h_x1; h_x1 = side_sb; h_y2 = h_y1; h_y1 = sh;
    sh = mh_b0*sh + mh_b1*h2_x1 + mh_b2*h2_x2 - mh_a1*h2_y1 - mh_a2*h2_y2;
    h2_x2 = h2_x1; h2_x1 = h_y1; h2_y2 = h2_y1; h2_y1 = sh;
    sh = mh_b0*sh + mh_b1*h3_x1 + mh_b2*h3_x2 - mh_a1*h3_y1 - mh_a2*h3_y2;
    h3_x2 = h3_x1; h3_x1 = h2_y1; h3_y2 = h3_y1; h3_y1 = sh;
    sh = mh_b0*sh + mh_b1*h4_x1 + mh_b2*h4_x2 - mh_a1*h4_y1 - mh_a2*h4_y2;
    h4_x2 = h4_x1; h4_x1 = h3_y1; h4_y2 = h4_y1; h4_y1 = sh;
    sh = mh_b0*sh + mh_b1*h5_x1 + mh_b2*h5_x2 - mh_a1*h5_y1 - mh_a2*h5_y2;
    h5_x2 = h5_x1; h5_x1 = h4_y1; h5_y2 = h5_y1; h5_y1 = sh;
    sh = mh_b0*sh + mh_b1*h6_x1 + mh_b2*h6_x2 - mh_a1*h6_y1 - mh_a2*h6_y2;
    h6_x2 = h6_x1; h6_x1 = h5_y1; h6_y2 = h6_y1; h6_y1 = sh;
    // smooth mono blend (click-free engage/disengage)
    bamt += (mono_t - bamt)*sm_gain;
    side_out = side_sb + (sh - side_sb)*bamt;
    r0 = mid_sb + side_out;
    r1 = mid_sb - side_out;

    // sub enhance: one-pole low shelf @55 Hz blended into the band
    enh_g += (enh_g_t - enh_g)*sm_gain;
    e_0 += (1-c_lp55)*(r0 - e_0);
    e_1 += (1-c_lp55)*(r1 - e_1);
    b0 = r0 + enh_g*e_0;
    b1 = r1 + enh_g*e_1;

    // tight: differential-envelope transient shaper on the sub band
    mid = (b0 + b1)*0.5;
    ea = abs(mid);
    ef += (ea - ef)*sm_5ms;
    es += (ef - es)*sm_50ms;
    tr = ef - es;
    tr = max(0, tr - 0.03*es);     // relative threshold kills ripple
    kk = 1 + punch01*2.5*min(tr/(es + 0.0001), 0.8);
    kk = min(max(kk, 0.6), 1.6);
    b0 *= kk; b1 *= kk;

    // perfect-reconstruction mix: explicit LR4 highs + processed lows
    y0 = h0 + b0;
    y1 = h1 + b1;
  );

  //================ AIR section ================
  air_byp ? (
    z0 = y0; z1 = y1;
  ) : (
    // harshness detector: bandpassed mid, fast/slow envelope
    mid2 = (y0 + y1)*0.5;
    bp = p_b0*mid2 + p_b1*p_x1 + p_b2*p_x2 - p_a1*p_y1 - p_a2*p_y2;
    p_x2 = p_x1; p_x1 = mid2; p_y2 = p_y1; p_y1 = bp;
    ha = abs(bp);
    harsh += (ha - harsh)*(ha > harsh ? sm_1ms : sm_113ms);
    harsh_thr = inst_mode ? 0.0251 : 0.0631;  // Inst: -32 dBFS | Bus: -24 dBFS (v1.6.0)
    over = max(0, harsh - harsh_thr);
    // -- v1.6.0 Clean law: zone-shaped authority x AIR gate x mode ceiling
    // Knob zones (internal only): SOFT 0-50% -> auth 0.30,
    // MID 50-83% -> 0.70, HARD 83-100% -> 1.00 (piecewise, no cliff)
    cz = clean01;
    cauth = cz < 0.5 ? cz*0.6 :
            cz < 0.833333 ? 0.3 + (cz-0.5)*1.2 :
                            0.7 + (cz-0.833333)*1.8;
    // AIR gate: Clean starts policing the boost once AIR passes its
    // half (+3 dB); authority ramps in with a smoothstep knee centred
    // on the half, full by +4 dB. Below the knee Clean is inert.
    gauth = min(max((air_db - 2.5)*0.666667, 0), 1);
    gauth = gauth*gauth*(3 - 2*gauth);
    // Mode ceiling: INST may eat the whole boost on harsh peaks;
    // BUS caps at 3 dB - "hard" but delicate, a bus/master stays safe
    cap_db = inst_mode ? air_db : min(air_db, 3);
    red_t = min(cap_db, cauth*gauth*over*24);
    red_db += (red_t - red_db)*(red_t > red_db ? sm_fast : sm_gain);

    // smooth air shelf: dry + g * one-pole-highpassed, g follows Clean
    g_air = 2.1*(10^((air_db - red_db)/20) - 1);
    h_0 = c_hp8k*(h_0 + y0 - hx_0); hx_0 = y0;
    h_1 = c_hp8k*(h_1 + y1 - hx_1); hx_1 = y1;
    z0 = y0 + g_air*h_0;
    z1 = y1 + g_air*h_1;
  );

  // Report combined gain reduction to REAPER's mixer/TCP meters.
  // (moved to the end of @sample, next to the output limiter)

  //================ VINTAGE DRIVE ================
  // Skipped entirely unless drive is dialed in: the neutral path stays
  // bit-transparent (and latency-free). When engaged, the saturation runs
  // at 2x (short FIR oversampling) and the wet path is delay-compensated
  // so the dry/wet blend stays phase-coherent.
  (drv_on && drv01 > 0) ? (
    // click-free engagement: smooth the wet blend and the push
    drvw += (drvw_t - drvw)*sm_gain;
    drvpush += (drvpush_t - drvpush)*sm_gain;

    //--- band split (coherent with Sub Enhance @160 Hz / Air @8 kHz)
    drv_focus == 0 ? (
      // SUB: LR4 lowpass @160 Hz (reuses s_ coeffs, own states)
      t = s_b0*z0 + s_b1*dl_x1_0 + s_b2*dl_x2_0 - s_a1*dl_y1_0 - s_a2*dl_y2_0;
      dl_x2_0 = dl_x1_0; dl_x1_0 = z0; dl_y2_0 = dl_y1_0; dl_y1_0 = t;
      db0 = s_b0*t + s_b1*dl2_x1_0 + s_b2*dl2_x2_0 - s_a1*dl2_y1_0 - s_a2*dl2_y2_0;
      dl2_x2_0 = dl2_x1_0; dl2_x1_0 = t; dl2_y2_0 = dl2_y1_0; dl2_y1_0 = db0;
      t = s_b0*z1 + s_b1*dl_x1_1 + s_b2*dl_x2_1 - s_a1*dl_y1_1 - s_a2*dl_y2_1;
      dl_x2_1 = dl_x1_1; dl_x1_1 = z1; dl_y2_1 = dl_y1_1; dl_y1_1 = t;
      db1 = s_b0*t + s_b1*dl2_x1_1 + s_b2*dl2_x2_1 - s_a1*dl2_y1_1 - s_a2*dl2_y2_1;
      dl2_x2_1 = dl2_x1_1; dl2_x1_1 = t; dl2_y2_1 = dl2_y1_1; dl2_y1_1 = db1;
    ) : drv_focus == 2 ? (
      // AIR: one-pole highpass @8 kHz (same corner as the Air shelf)
      db0 = c_hp8k*(dah_0 + z0 - dahx_0); dahx_0 = z0; dah_0 = db0;
      db1 = c_hp8k*(dah_1 + z1 - dahx_1); dahx_1 = z1; dah_1 = db1;
    ) : (
      // FULL: whole spectrum
      db0 = z0; db1 = z1;
    );

    //--- ch0: polyphase 2x upsample -> saturate -> polyphase downsample
    // 17-tap halfband: even phase is just the center tap (scaled delay)
    ye0 = df8*dux3_0;
    yo0 = df1*db0 + df3*dux0_0 + df5*dux1_0 + df7*dux2_0 + df9*dux3_0 +
          df11*dux4_0 + df13*dux5_0 + df15*dux6_0;
    dux6_0 = dux5_0; dux5_0 = dux4_0; dux4_0 = dux3_0; dux3_0 = dux2_0;
    dux2_0 = dux1_0; dux1_0 = dux0_0; dux0_0 = db0;
    // saturate at 2x (x2 compensates the polyphase half-gain)
    se0 = drv_sat(2*ye0);
    so0 = drv_sat(2*yo0);
    // downsample: halfband FIR across the interleaved 2x phases
    de0 = df1*dso0_0 + df3*dso1_0 + df5*dso2_0 + df7*dso3_0 + df8*dse3_0 +
          df9*dso4_0 + df11*dso5_0 + df13*dso6_0 + df15*dso7_0;
    dse7_0 = dse6_0; dse6_0 = dse5_0; dse5_0 = dse4_0; dse4_0 = dse3_0;
    dse3_0 = dse2_0; dse2_0 = dse1_0; dse1_0 = dse0_0; dse0_0 = se0;
    dso7_0 = dso6_0; dso6_0 = dso5_0; dso5_0 = dso4_0; dso4_0 = dso3_0;
    dso3_0 = dso2_0; dso2_0 = dso1_0; dso1_0 = dso0_0; dso0_0 = so0;
    // DC block (asymmetry creates DC)
    ds0 = de0 - ddc_x0 + ddc_r*ddc_y0; ddc_x0 = de0; ddc_y0 = ds0;

    //--- ch1: same
    ye1 = df8*dux3_1;
    yo1 = df1*db1 + df3*dux0_1 + df5*dux1_1 + df7*dux2_1 + df9*dux3_1 +
          df11*dux4_1 + df13*dux5_1 + df15*dux6_1;
    dux6_1 = dux5_1; dux5_1 = dux4_1; dux4_1 = dux3_1; dux3_1 = dux2_1;
    dux2_1 = dux1_1; dux1_1 = dux0_1; dux0_1 = db1;
    se1 = drv_sat(2*ye1);
    so1 = drv_sat(2*yo1);
    de1 = df1*dso0_1 + df3*dso1_1 + df5*dso2_1 + df7*dso3_1 + df8*dse3_1 +
          df9*dso4_1 + df11*dso5_1 + df13*dso6_1 + df15*dso7_1;
    dse7_1 = dse6_1; dse6_1 = dse5_1; dse5_1 = dse4_1; dse4_1 = dse3_1;
    dse3_1 = dse2_1; dse2_1 = dse1_1; dse1_1 = dse0_1; dse0_1 = se1;
    dso7_1 = dso6_1; dso6_1 = dso5_1; dso5_1 = dso4_1; dso4_1 = dso3_1;
    dso3_1 = dso2_1; dso2_1 = dso1_1; dso1_1 = dso0_1; dso0_1 = so1;
    ds1 = de1 - ddc_x1 + ddc_r*ddc_y1; ddc_x1 = de1; ddc_y1 = ds1;

    //--- delay-compensate dry + band by the FIR latency (4 samples @1x)
    zd0 = dzz3_0;
    dzz3_0 = dzz2_0; dzz2_0 = dzz1_0; dzz1_0 = dzz0_0; dzz0_0 = z0;
    bd0 = dbb3_0;
    dbb3_0 = dbb2_0; dbb2_0 = dbb1_0; dbb1_0 = dbb0_0; dbb0_0 = db0;
    zd1 = dzz3_1;
    dzz3_1 = dzz2_1; dzz2_1 = dzz1_1; dzz1_1 = dzz0_1; dzz0_1 = z1;
    bd1 = dbb3_1;
    dbb3_1 = dbb2_1; dbb2_1 = dbb1_1; dbb1_1 = dbb0_1; dbb0_1 = db1;

    //--- wet/dry: add only the saturation difference (transparent at w=0)
    z0 = zd0 + drvw*(ds0 - bd0);
    z1 = zd1 + drvw*(ds1 - bd1);
  );

  //--- output trim + sanitise
  out_g += (out_t - out_g)*sm_gain;
  o0 = z0*out_g; o1 = z1*out_g;
  o0 = o0 != o0 ? 0 : min(max(o0, -4), 4);
  o1 = o1 != o1 ? 0 : min(max(o1, -4), 4);
  //--- LOW CUT (v1.7.0): TPT/SVF highpass on the summed signal - the
  // last word before the safety limiter, so the limiter stops
  // reacting to infrasonics and drive-generated DC. Coefficients,
  // damping and the 3rd-order blend slew together (~15 ms), and the
  // whole stage crossfades in/out (~10 ms): stepping the knob or
  // flipping BUS/INST never clicks. slider17 = 0 is an exact bypass:
  // once the mix reaches zero the states prime on the input, so
  // re-engaging starts from steady state.
  lc_g += (lc_g_t - lc_g)*sm_lc;
  lc_k += (lc_k_t - lc_k)*sm_lc;
  lc_3m += ((lc_3rd ? 1 : 0) - lc_3m)*sm_lc;
  lc_mix += ((lc_on ? 1 : 0) - lc_mix)*sm_lcm;
  lc_mix > 0.0001 ? (
    lc_a1 = 1/(1 + lc_g*(lc_g + lc_k));
    lc_a2 = lc_g*lc_a1;
    lc_a3 = lc_g*lc_a2;
    lc_v3 = o0 - lc_ic2_0;
    lc_v1 = lc_a1*lc_ic1_0 + lc_a2*lc_v3;
    lc_v2 = lc_ic2_0 + lc_a2*lc_ic1_0 + lc_a3*lc_v3;
    lc_ic1_0 = 2*lc_v1 - lc_ic1_0;
    lc_ic2_0 = 2*lc_v2 - lc_ic2_0;
    lc_hp = o0 - lc_k*lc_v1 - lc_v2;
    lc_vv = lc_g*(lc_hp - lc_lp_0);
    lc_ylp = lc_lp_0 + lc_vv;
    lc_lp_0 = lc_ylp + lc_vv;
    lc_hp -= lc_3m*lc_ylp;
    o0 += (lc_hp - o0)*lc_mix;
    lc_v3 = o1 - lc_ic2_1;
    lc_v1 = lc_a1*lc_ic1_1 + lc_a2*lc_v3;
    lc_v2 = lc_ic2_1 + lc_a2*lc_ic1_1 + lc_a3*lc_v3;
    lc_ic1_1 = 2*lc_v1 - lc_ic1_1;
    lc_ic2_1 = 2*lc_v2 - lc_ic2_1;
    lc_hp = o1 - lc_k*lc_v1 - lc_v2;
    lc_vv = lc_g*(lc_hp - lc_lp_1);
    lc_ylp = lc_lp_1 + lc_vv;
    lc_lp_1 = lc_ylp + lc_vv;
    lc_hp -= lc_3m*lc_ylp;
    o1 += (lc_hp - o1)*lc_mix;
  ) : (
    lc_ic1_0 = 0; lc_ic2_0 = o0; lc_lp_0 = 0;
    lc_ic1_1 = 0; lc_ic2_1 = o1; lc_lp_1 = 0;
  );
  //--- output safety limiter: fixed -1 dBFS ceiling on the FINAL output.
  // Sits after the output trim: with Safety ON the plugin can never clip,
  // no matter how hard the sub/air/drive stages are pushed.
  pk = max(abs(o0), abs(o1));
  tgt = (safety_on && pk > 0.891250938) ? 0.891250938/pk : 1;
  gr = tgt < gr ? tgt : gr + (tgt - gr)*sm_100ms;  // instant atk / 100 ms rel
  o0 *= gr; o1 *= gr;
  gr_disp += (gr - gr_disp)*sm_fast;
  // report combined GR (limiter + de-harsh) to REAPER's mixer/TCP meters:
  // ext_gr_meter is REAPER's documented mechanism, value in dB, <= 0
  ext_gr_meter = min(0, 20*log10(max(gr, 0.00000001)) - red_t);
  //--- startup fade: 15 ms ramp on load/insert masks the cold-start
  // transient (limiter gr slams from 1 on the first hot sample; filter
  // states charge from zero). Inaudible, runs once per @init.
  startup = min(1, startup + 1/(0.015*srate));
  o0 *= startup; o1 *= startup;
  m_out = max(m_out*mdec, max(abs(o0), abs(o1)));
  vu_pk = max(abs(o0), abs(o1));
  vu_out_sm = max(vu_pk, vu_out_sm*vu_rel);   // true peak hold + 150ms decay
  //--- POWER bypass con crossfade de 25ms (click-free)
  // bypass_mix: 0=wet (POWER ON), 1=dry (POWER OFF)
  bypass_target = (slider15 > 0.5) ? 0 : 1;
  bypass_mix += (bypass_target - bypass_mix) * min(1, 1/(0.025*srate));
  spl0 = o0*(1-bypass_mix) + dry0*bypass_mix;
  spl1 = o1*(1-bypass_mix) + dry1*bypass_mix;

  cnt += 1;
  cnt >= 1024 ? ( cnt = 0; flush_all(); );

//---------------------------------------------------------------- @gfx
//---------------------------------------------------------------- @gfx - Juan's PSD design (fixed 951x623, plate = window)
@gfx 951 623
  //--- POWER OFF: VU con apagado gradual (el bypass de audio está en @sample)
  slider15 < 0.5 ? (
    m_in *= 0.999; m_out *= 0.999; m_gr *= 0.999;
    gr_disp = max(gr_disp*0.999, 0.0000001);
  );
  g_px0 = 0; g_py0 = 0;
  gfx_blit(0, 1, 0, 0,0,951,623, 0,0,951,623);

  g_mx = mouse_x - g_px0; g_my = mouse_y - g_py0;
  g_mc = mouse_cap & 1;

  //================ mouse ================
  g_mc && !g_lmc ? (
    g_drag = -1;
    // toggles (2-pos): 0=SUB BYPASS 1=SAFETY 2=AIR BYPASS 3=DRIVE POWER
    g_t = 0; while (g_t < 4) (
      g_tx = g_t==0 ? 147 : g_t==1 ? 364 : g_t==2 ? 590 : 699;
      g_mx >= g_tx-48 && g_mx < g_tx+48 && g_my >= 520 && g_my < 576 ? (
        g_t==0 ? ( slider2 = 1-(slider2>0.5); sliderchange(2); ) :
        g_t==1 ? ( slider6 = 1-(slider6>0.5); sliderchange(6); ) :
        g_t==2 ? ( slider7 = 1-(slider7>0.5); sliderchange(7); ) :
                 ( slider13 = 1-(slider13>0.5); sliderchange(13); );
        upd_params();
      );
      g_t += 1;
    );
    // MODE 3-pos drag (LO-MID/FULL/HI-MID -> Drive Focus Sub/Full/Air)
    g_mx >= 812.5-48 && g_mx < 812.5+48 && g_my >= 520 && g_my < 576 ? (
      g_modedrag = 1;
    );
    // IN/GR/OUT LED radio (only one active)
    g_b = 0; while (g_b < 3) (
      g_bx = g_b==0 ? 447 : g_b==1 ? 476.5 : 505.5;
      (g_mx-g_bx)*(g_mx-g_bx)+(g_my-379)*(g_my-379) < 14*14 ? (
        slider14 = g_b;  // 0=IN, 1=GR, 2=OUT (direct)
        sliderchange(14);
      );
      g_b += 1;
    );
    // POWER toggle (vertical: up=ON, down=OFF)
    (g_mx-480.5)*(g_mx-480.5)+(g_my-487)*(g_my-487) < 32*32 ? (
      slider15 = slider15 > 0.5 ? 0 : 1;
      sliderchange(15);
    );
    // OPERATION toggle (horizontal: left=BUS, right=INST)
    // Simétrico al LED DE-HARSH (904,300) -> (120,300)
    g_mx >= 74-48 && g_mx < 74+48 && g_my >= 256.5-48 && g_my < 256.5+48 ? (
      slider16 = slider16 > 0.5 ? 0 : 1;
      sliderchange(16);
      upd_params();
    );
    // knobs (drag)
    g_k = 0; while (g_k < 9) (
      hit_knob2(g_mx,g_my,kcx(g_k),kcy(g_k)) ? (
        (mouse_cap & 12) ? kset(g_k, kdef(g_k)) : (
          g_drag = g_k; gd_y0 = g_my; gd_v0 = kval(g_k);
        );
      );
      g_k += 1;
    );
  );
  g_mc && g_drag >= 0 ? (
    kset(g_drag, gd_v0 + (gd_y0-g_my)/150*(kmax(g_drag)-kmin(g_drag)));
  );
  g_mc && g_modedrag ? (
    g_mp = g_mx < 812.5-25 ? 0 : g_mx > 812.5+25 ? 2 : 1;
    g_mp != slider12 ? (
      slider12 = g_mp; sliderchange(12); upd_params();
    );
  );
  !g_mc ? ( g_drag = -1; g_modedrag = 0; );
  g_lmc = g_mc;

  //================ mouse wheel (v1.6.0, polished) ================
  // Every knob and lever answers to the wheel; the IN/GR/OUT LED radio
  // is the ONLY exclusion (click-only). ONE physical notch (delta 120)
  // = ONE step: the delta accumulates across frames (hi-res wheels
  // included) and each full 120 counts once, so stepped controls never
  // skip positions. Levers are DIRECTIONAL, never flipping: wheel up
  // drives a lever to its "1" end, wheel down to its "0" end, and
  // further scrolling in the same direction simply holds it there.
  // "End" means the DRAWN handle end (up = right / up), so SAFETY -
  // whose slider is inverted in the drawing - maps opposite in value.
  g_wh = mouse_wheel; mouse_wheel = 0;
  // hover target: 1..8 = knobs (id+1), 20=MODE, 21=OPERATION, 22=POWER,
  // 23..26 = bottom toggles (SUB BYPASS / SAFETY / AIR BYPASS / DRIVE PWR)
  g_wtgt = 0;
  g_k = 0;
  while (g_k < 9 && g_wtgt == 0) (
    hit_knob2(g_mx, g_my, kcx(g_k), kcy(g_k)) ? g_wtgt = g_k + 1;
    g_k += 1;
  );
  (g_wtgt == 0 && g_mx >= 812.5-48 && g_mx < 812.5+48 && g_my >= 520 && g_my < 576) ? g_wtgt = 20;
  (g_wtgt == 0 && g_mx >= 74-48 && g_mx < 74+48 && g_my >= 208 && g_my < 304) ? g_wtgt = 21;
  (g_wtgt == 0 && (g_mx-480.5)*(g_mx-480.5) + (g_my-487)*(g_my-487) < 32*32) ? g_wtgt = 22;
  (g_wtgt == 0 && g_mx >= 147-48 && g_mx < 147+48 && g_my >= 520 && g_my < 576) ? g_wtgt = 23;
  (g_wtgt == 0 && g_mx >= 364-48 && g_mx < 364+48 && g_my >= 520 && g_my < 576) ? g_wtgt = 24;
  (g_wtgt == 0 && g_mx >= 590-48 && g_mx < 590+48 && g_my >= 520 && g_my < 576) ? g_wtgt = 25;
  (g_wtgt == 0 && g_mx >= 699-48 && g_mx < 699+48 && g_my >= 520 && g_my < 576) ? g_wtgt = 26;
  g_wtgt != g_wlast ? ( g_wacc = 0; g_wlast = g_wtgt; );  // no cross-control leaks
  (g_drag >= 0 || g_modedrag) ? g_wacc = 0 : g_wacc += g_wh;
  g_wn = floor(abs(g_wacc)/120);                          // whole notches pending
  (g_wn > 0 && g_wtgt > 0) ? (
    g_wdir = g_wacc > 0 ? 1 : -1;
    g_wn2 = min(g_wn, 3);                                 // steps applied per frame
    g_wacc -= g_wn*120*g_wdir;                            // consume all counted notches
    g_wtgt <= 9 ? (
      g_k = g_wtgt - 1;
      g_wstep = (g_k==7 || g_k==8) ? 1 : g_k==5 ? 0.2 : (g_k==0 || g_k==1) ? 0.5 : 2;
      kset(g_k, kval(g_k) + g_wdir*g_wn2*g_wstep);
    ) : g_wtgt == 20 ? (
      // MODE 3-pos: one position per notch, through the centre, clamped
      slider12 = min(max((slider12|0) + g_wdir*g_wn2, 0), 2);
      sliderchange(12); upd_params();
    ) : g_wtgt == 21 ? (
      g_wval = g_wdir > 0 ? 1 : 0;
      g_wval != (slider16 > 0.5) ? ( slider16 = g_wval; sliderchange(16); upd_params(); );
    ) : g_wtgt == 22 ? (
      g_wval = g_wdir > 0 ? 1 : 0;
      g_wval != (slider15 > 0.5) ? ( slider15 = g_wval; sliderchange(15); );
    ) : (
      g_wval = g_wdir > 0 ? 1 : 0;
      g_wtgt == 23 ? ( g_wval != (slider2 > 0.5) ? ( slider2 = g_wval; sliderchange(2); upd_params(); ); ) :
      // SAFETY is drawn inverted (frame 1/right = slider6 0): the wheel
      // follows the DRAWN handle - up = right, down = left - like DRIVE PWR
      g_wtgt == 24 ? ( (1 - g_wval) != (slider6 > 0.5) ? ( slider6 = 1 - g_wval; sliderchange(6); upd_params(); ); ) :
      g_wtgt == 25 ? ( g_wval != (slider7 > 0.5) ? ( slider7 = g_wval; sliderchange(7); upd_params(); ); ) :
                       ( g_wval != (slider13 > 0.5) ? ( slider13 = g_wval; sliderchange(13); upd_params(); ); );
    );
  );

  //================ draw ================
  g_k = 0; while (g_k < 9) ( draw_knob(g_k); g_k += 1; );
  draw_tog2(147, 548.5, slider2>0.5 ? 1 : 0);
  draw_tog2(364, 547.5, slider6<0.5 ? 1 : 0);
  draw_tog2(590, 547.5, slider7>0.5 ? 1 : 0);
  draw_tog2(699, 547.5, slider13>0.5 ? 1 : 0);
  gfx_blit(7, 1, 0, 0, (slider12|0)*128, 128, 128, g_px0+812-44, g_py0+548-43.3, 87.3, 87.3);

  // VU: off image when POWER off, else face + needle
  (slider15 > 0.5) ? (
    gfx_blit(8, 1, 0, 0,0,218,218, g_px0+366.5, g_py0+101.5, 218,218);
  ) : (
    gfx_blit(12, 1, 0, 0,0,218,218, g_px0+366.5, g_py0+101.5, 218,218);
  );
  slider14==0 ? g_vdb = 20*log10(max(vu_in_sm,0.0000001)) :
  slider14==1 ? g_vdb = 20*log10(max(gr_disp,0.0000001)) - red_db :
                g_vdb = 20*log10(max(vu_out_sm,0.0000001));
  g_vdb = min(max(g_vdb,-20),3);
  g_vdb <= 0 ? g_vang_t = 171-(g_vdb+20)*4.05 : g_vang_t = 90-g_vdb*26.333;
  g_vang_t > g_vang ? g_vk = 0.75 : g_vk = 0.35;
  g_vang += (g_vang_t - g_vang)*g_vk;
  g_var = g_vang*$pi/180;
  (slider15 > 0.5) ? (
    g_vpx = g_px0+475.5; g_vpy = g_py0+231.5;
    gfx_set(0.10,0.08,0.06);
    gfx_line(g_vpx, g_vpy, g_vpx+95*cos(g_var), g_vpy-95*sin(g_var), 1);
    gfx_set(0.16,0.13,0.10); gfx_circle(g_vpx, g_vpy, 9, 1, 1);
    gfx_set(0.55,0.48,0.38); gfx_circle(g_vpx-2, g_vpy-2, 3, 1, 1);
  );

  // IN/GR/OUT LEDs: 2-frame (0=off, 1=on), radio behavior
  g_b = 0; while (g_b < 3) (
    g_bx = g_b==0 ? 447 : g_b==1 ? 476.5 : 505.5;
    g_led_fr = ((slider15 > 0.5) && (slider14 == g_b)) ? 1 : 0;
    gfx_blit(10, 1, 0, 0, g_led_fr*20, 20, 20, g_px0+g_bx-10, g_py0+379-10, 20, 20);
    g_b += 1;
  );
  // DE-HARSH LED (v1.6.0): eager "placebo" law - lights early and climbs
  // fast with detector activity (g_dh_over) and real reduction (red_db),
  // scaled by knob position. Deliberately livelier than the gentle DSP
  // reduction behind it: the show is visual, the audio stays respectful.
  g_dh_over = max(0, harsh - (inst_mode ? 0.0251 : 0.0631));
  g_dh_act = min(1, (red_db*0.5 + g_dh_over*1.6) * (0.30 + 0.70*clean01));
  g_dh_target = (slider15 > 0.5 && m_in > 0.001 && (red_db > 0.001 || g_dh_over > 0.002)) ? g_dh_act*127 : 0;
  g_fdh += (g_dh_target - g_fdh) * 0.25;
  gfx_blit(11, 1, 0, 0, floor(max(0,min(127,g_fdh)))*48, 48, 48, g_px0+859-23.5, g_py0+258.5-23.5, 47, 47);
  // OPERATION lever (2-pos horizontal, img 6): 0=BUS(left) 1=INST(right)
  draw_tog2(74, 256.5, slider16>0.5?1:0);
  // MODE/BUS/INST labels are in the panel PNG (Juan's design)
  // POWER toggle (up=ON, down=OFF)
  gfx_blit(9, 1, 0, 0, (slider15>0.5?0:1)*128, 128, 128, g_px0+436.7, g_py0+443.4, 87.3, 87.3);
